ation of enzyme activity. Rarely patients have been found to have an odd odor or neurological disorders such as brain demyelination.\" [Orphanet:168598]\nsubset: clingen {source=\"MONDO:CLINGEN\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0008397\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C123435\"}\nsubset: ncit_rare {source=\"NCIT:C123435\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:250850\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:168598\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:168598\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:168598\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"brain demyelination due to methionine adenosyltransferase deficiency\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40011/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5655-9589]\nsynonym: \"hypermethioninemia, persistent, autosomal dominant, due to methionine adenosyltransferase I/III deficiency\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"isolated persistent hypermethioninemia\" EXACT [NCIT:C123435]\nsynonym: \"MAT deficiency\" EXACT [NCIT:C123435, OMIM:250850]\nsynonym: \"MAT I/III deficiency\" EXACT [NCIT:C123435, OMIM:250850, Orphanet:168598]\nsynonym: \"methionine adenosyltransferase deficiency\" EXACT [NCIT:C123435] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"methionine adenosyltransferase deficiency, autosomal recessive\" EXACT []\nxref: GARD:0008397 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:E72.1 {source=\"Orphanet:168598\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:75700 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: NCIT:C123435 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: OMIM:250850 {source=\"Orphanet:168598\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:168598/e\"}\nxref: Orphanet:168598 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"OMIM:250850\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0268621 {source=\"MEDGEN:75700\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005066 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C123435\", source=\"Or